\f1\fs22 \'91Nice lounge,\'92 Tony remarked. It wasn\'92t showy, but Tony could tell it had been designed and furnished on a limitless budget.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, this is just the reception room,\'92 Fisher explained.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Reception room? Like a waiting room?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No. A place to hold receptions: cocktail parties, board meetings, corporate executions \'85 sometimes all at once.\'92 Fisher smiled in that trademark lopsided Elvi way. \'91Not that we\'92ve had a corporate execution for some time.\'92 Fisher smiled. \'91There are other more private spaces for sir to relax.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Fisher directed Tony past the bar to a corridor that doubled back behind the left wells. \'91There\'92s a modest bathroom through the door at the end. I\'92ll arrange a fresh change of clothes while you wash. Does sir have anything in mind?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, um \'85 just something I wouldn\'92t seem out of place drinking beer in.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Very good, sir. In the meantime, I will assemble the staff for sir\'92s inspection.\'92 Fisher turned to go about his tasks.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony crossed his eyebrows in confusion. \'91You know, other Elvi call me the Great Teacher.\'92 He was surprised to discover he felt a bit miffed that Fisher had not addressed him as he\'92d come to welcome.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Impressive, sir. What is it you teach?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony thought on that. \'91How to get out of a tight situation, mostly,\'92 he said, thinking his lyric-writing abilities were at their best when he needed to save his own skin. Or when he was class to Sarah and Little Clinton.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91A survivalist. Magnificent,\'92 Fisher said, possibly in mock appreciation. \'91I suspect the blood of the Jamison Hardy flows strong in your veins.\'92
